index fb7245d6bc19e984738226bec23fcb80716d62b1..80d1779c62ef55c0112766a04b4a061aca305743 100644
--- a/docs/developers/hostname_filter.md
+++ b/docs/developers/hostname_filter.md
@@ -92,6 +92,32 @@ The following are always allowed regardless of domain settings:
 - Mailto links: `mailto:user@example.com`
 - Protocol-relative URLs: `//example.com/page`
 
+## JSON and Structured Output
+
+JSON payloads are detected automatically and filtered without corrupting their structure. This covers responses requested with a structured output schema (`ChatInput::setChatStructuredJsonSchema()`), prompt-engineered JSON, and JSON documents inside tool call arguments. Two payload shapes are recognized:
+
+- Text that is wholly a JSON object or array (surrounding whitespace allowed).
+- A single fenced code block (```` ```json ```` with optional surrounding prose, or a bare ```` ``` ```` fence surrounded only by whitespace) whose content is a JSON object or array.
+
+Instead of pushing the whole payload through the HTML pipeline — which would entity-encode it beyond decoding — every string value (and object key) is filtered individually with the same Markdown and HTML rules. If nothing in the payload violates the allowlist, the payload is returned byte-for-byte. If a violation is found, the offending values are filtered and the payload is re-encoded; formatting and whitespace inside the JSON are not preserved in that case, but the result always decodes with `json_decode()`.
+
+Filtering precedence is: full trust mode, then plain text mode, then JSON detection, then the regular Markdown/HTML pipeline. Bare URLs in JSON string values follow the same policy as bare URLs in prose: they are only stripped in plain text mode.
+
+### JSON Mode
+
+When a chat response is requested with a structured output schema, the provider proxy additionally puts the filter in JSON mode for that response. In JSON mode a payload that fails to decode (malformed or truncated JSON) is filtered as plain text instead of as HTML, so its structure is never entity-encoded. You can control this per request:
+
+```php
+use Drupal\ai\Dto\HostnameFilterDto;
+
+$input = new ChatInput([...]);
+// Force JSON mode (or pass jsonMode: FALSE to suppress the automatic
+// enabling for structured output responses).
+$input->setHostnameFilter(new HostnameFilterDto(jsonMode: TRUE));
+```
+
+Streamed structured output responses are filtered chunk by chunk in plain text mode, because partial JSON fragments cannot be decoded.
+
 ## Images
 
 Images with disallowed domains are always completely removed (the entire `<img>` tag or `![alt](url)` markdown). Rewrite mode only affects links, not images.
